  "surface_observations": [
    "The three-storey frontage has a continuous shallow stepped parapet line, unbroken over the 174 gate. The obliques show no exposed roof tile surface above the parapet.",
    "On the second storey a painted horizontal louvre box projects immediately left of the central upper sash, between the centre sash and the northern pair. The southern sash pair has a small bare white air conditioner at its first window only. Another louvre box sits further north of the pair.",
    "Additional louvre boxes are below the upper sash row. Detached wire clothes-drying frames and hanging items can cover the sill and roof in obliques. Single-pixel exposed details behind foliage are not usable as fixed structural points."
  ],
  "normalization": "The unobstructed front camera supplies the actual window sill at 5.1 m. Both oblique roof observations report the unadjusted height separately and the differential against the same sill in each image. This removes a roughly 1 m opposite-sign station elevation bias. Absolute eave height is an estimate."
